==Enemy==
Dark Cyclone has short range, medium movement speed and extremely high DPS, but its damage per hit is relatively low. Like many Dark enemies, it also has numerous knockbacks, with 10.

==Strategy==
[[:Category:Cyclones|Cyclone]]s are notoriously weak to crowd-control, and that goes double for Dark Cyclone. With two easily countered traits, any combination of [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] and/or [[:Category:Anti-Dark Cats|anti-Dark]] units with slow or freeze abilities can put an end to Dark Cyclone's onslaught, some examples being [[Flower Cat (Special Cat)|Flower Cat]], [[Cat Gunslinger (Rare Cat)|Cat Gunslinger]], [[Bodhisattva Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Bodhisattva Cat]], [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Bishop Cat]] and [[Oda Nobunaga (Uber Rare Cat)|Oda Nobunaga]]. Stack cheap attackers like [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Salon Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] to keep the peons at bay, but do stay mindful of the [[Dark Emperor Nyandam|Nyandam]] in [[Attack on D-Cyclone (Expert)|Attack on D-Cyclone]] and [[Wrath of D-Cyclone (Insane)|Wrath of D-Cyclone]] and the [[Director Kurosawah|Kurosawah]] in [[Doom Paradise (Insane)|Doom Paradise]], for Dark Cyclone's knockbacks can easily draw your units into the backliner's range.

